<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  dev.disksentinel.scan: the bounded, read-only investigation, retried until it completes.

  install path: ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.disksentinel.scan.plist
  laid by: infra/macos/tools/disk-sentinel/install.sh, which renders ${HOME}
  measured by: bin/idp-inventory, plane mac (MANAGED when this file name is tracked)

  Why every 30 minutes instead of 03:15 once a day (2026-11-05): a single daily slot with a
  load precheck meant a workstation busy at 03:15 skipped the inventory entirely, and the
  founder saw "review" with no data and no way to tell a deferral from a failure. The job now
  asks every 30 minutes; the script itself decides - it returns early when a COMPLETE inventory
  is under 24 hours old, records DEFERRED when load is high and PARTIAL when a directory timed
  out, and only a COMPLETE stamps the 24-hour clock. The retry costs one launchd wake and a
  load check, not a second traversal.

  StartInterval does not fire while the Mac sleeps, so this is not a wall-clock guarantee; it
  is the retry that replaces "wait until tomorrow".
-->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
<key>Label</key><string>dev.disksentinel.scan</string>
<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/bin/bash</string><string>${HOME}/.local/share/disk-sentinel/sentinel.sh</string><string>scan</string><string>--auto</string></array>
<key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
<key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
<key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
<key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
<key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/dev/null</string><key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/dev/null</string>
</dict></plist>
